  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Al Quds Human Rights Clinic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Irish Representative Office in Ramallah, through the HoMs Fund, will support a six-month field-research project will document the gendered impact of the coercive environment facing Bedouin women in the E1 area. Two female Bedouin graduates will be hired and trained as a field researcher to conduct interviews, collect testimonies, and access hard-to-reach communities where movement restrictions prevent regular health clinic access. The study will produce evidence-based analysis on how forced displacement, limited mobility, and loss of educational opportunities affect Bedouin women, which would facilitate supporting future advocacy, protection interventions, and gender-sensitive policy responses.</narrative>
  </description>
